<% content_for :title, "Does starting valuation predict a safe withdrawal rate? | 4% Rule Calculator" %>
<% content_for :description, "Retirements that started when stocks were expensive, measured by Shiller's CAPE, supported much lower withdrawal rates, and today's CAPE is higher than any start year in the data." %>

<%
  today = @analysis.today
  highest = @analysis.highest_start
  points = @analysis.points
  in_progress_top = @analysis.in_progress_points.max_by { |point| point[:cape] }
%>

<%# Header %>
<header class="sticky top-0 z-50 w-full bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-gray-200">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 h-16">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 min-w-0">
        <%= render "calculator/logo_mark" %>
        <%= link_to root_path, class: "hidden sm:inline text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#1F2937] hover:text-[#7C3AED] transition-colors" do %>
          The 4% Rule Calculator
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <nav class="shrink-0 flex items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6">
        <%= link_to "Calculator", root_path, class: "text-sm font-medium text-[#6B7280] hover:text-[#7C3AED] transition-colors" %>
        <span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#7C3AED]">Valuations</span>
        <%= link_to "Methodology", methodology_path, class: "text-sm font-medium text-[#6B7280] hover:text-[#7C3AED] transition-colors" %>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<%# Main Content %>
<main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 space-y-12">
  <section class="max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tight text-[#1F2937]">
      Does starting valuation predict a safe withdrawal rate?
    </h1>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-lg text-[#6B7280] max-w-2xl">
      <p>
        CAPE (the cyclically adjusted price-to-earnings ratio, or Shiller P/E10) is how many years of inflation-adjusted profit you pay for a share of the stock market.
        A CAPE of 20 means you pay 20 years of average earnings; a CAPE of 40 means 40.
      </p>
      <p>
        It matters for withdrawals because paying more for the same earnings tends to mean lower returns afterwards.
        Below, the chart compares the CAPE at the start of each year with what a retirement that began that year was worth 10 to 50 years later, and the table groups start years by CAPE.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#7C3AED]/5 border border-[#7C3AED]/10 p-6" data-today-callout>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7C3AED]">Today</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-3xl font-black text-[#1F2937]">
        CAPE in <%= Date.strptime(today[:as_of], "%Y-%m").strftime("%B %Y") %>: <%= number_with_precision(today[:cape], precision: 1) %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[#1F2937] leading-relaxed">
        Higher than <%= @analysis.percentile(today[:cape]) %>% of the <%= points.size %> start years (<%= points.first[:year] %> to <%= points.last[:year] %>) with a full 30-year record. The most expensive of those was <%= number_with_precision(highest[:cape], precision: 1) %>, in <%= link_to highest[:year], year_detail_path(highest[:year]), class: "text-[#7C3AED] font-medium hover:underline" %>.
        <% if in_progress_top && in_progress_top[:cape] > today[:cape] %>
          More recent retirements started at higher valuations but haven't reached 30 years yet: <%= link_to in_progress_top[:year], year_detail_path(in_progress_top[:year]), class: "text-[#7C3AED] font-medium hover:underline" %> began at <%= number_with_precision(in_progress_top[:cape], precision: 1) %>, above today, and its 4% withdrawal <%= in_progress_top[:four_percent_alive] ? "has lasted #{in_progress_top[:years_elapsed]} years so far" : "ran out" %>. Switch the chart below to a 10- or 20-year horizon to see how those years did.
        <% end %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm p-6"
           data-controller="valuation-timeline"
           data-valuation-timeline-data-value="<%= @analysis.timeline.to_json %>"
           data-valuation-timeline-initial-amount-value="1000000"
           data-valuation-timeline-horizon-value="30"
           data-valuation-timeline-scenarios-value="<%= Scenario::ALL.map { |sc| { key: sc.key, label: sc.label, color: sc.color, first_year: sc.first_year } }.to_json %>"
           data-valuation-timeline-data-through-value="<%= @analysis.data_through %>"
           data-valuation-timeline-events-value="<%= MarketEvents.all.to_json %>">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-3 mb-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2937]" data-valuation-timeline-target="title">Over time: valuation at the start vs. what <span data-valuation-timeline-target="horizonLabel">30</span> years left</h2>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <label for="timeline-horizon-select" class="text-sm font-medium text-[#6B7280]">Time Horizon:</label>
        <div class="relative">
          <select id="timeline-horizon-select"
                  aria-label="Time horizon"
                  class="appearance-none pl-3 pr-9 py-2 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-[#FAFAFA] text-[#1F2937] font-medium text-sm cursor-pointer hover:border-gray-400 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#7C3AED]/20 focus:border-[#7C3AED]"
                  data-valuation-timeline-target="dropdown"
                  data-action="change->valuation-timeline#changeHorizon">
            <% Calculator::MILESTONES.each do |years| %>
              <option value="<%= years %>" <%= "selected" if years == 30 %>><%= years %> years</option>
            <% end %>
          </select>
          <svg class="pointer-events-none absolute right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-4 h-4 text-[#6B7280]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#6B7280] mb-6">Lines: portfolio after <span data-valuation-timeline-target="horizonLabel">30</span> years, starting with $1,000,000 and withdrawing 4%, by investment mix. Grey: CAPE that January.</p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4" role="group" aria-label="Portfolios shown">
      <% Scenario::ALL.each do |scenario| %>
        <button type="button"
                data-valuation-timeline-target="chip"
                data-scenario="<%= scenario.key %>"
                data-action="valuation-timeline#toggleScenario"
                aria-pressed="false"
                data-color="<%= scenario.color %>"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border text-xs font-medium transition-colors border-gray-300 text-[#6B7280] bg-[#FAFAFA]">
          <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full" style="background-color: #D1D5DB"></span><%= scenario.label %>
        </button>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-[#6B7280]"></div>
        <span class="text-sm text-[#6B7280] whitespace-nowrap">CAPE at start</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <div class="w-3 h-3 bg-red-500/20"></div>
        <span class="text-sm text-[#6B7280] whitespace-nowrap">Below the starting amount</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <div class="h-3 border-l border-dashed border-[#6B7280]"></div>
        <span class="text-sm text-[#6B7280] whitespace-nowrap">Major market event</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative w-full" style="height: 400px;">
      <canvas data-valuation-timeline-target="canvas"></canvas>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2937] mb-4">Outcomes by starting CAPE</h2>
    <p class="text-[#6B7280] mb-4">Highest first-year rate that lasted 30 years, grouped by the CAPE when each retirement started. 100% S&amp;P 500, no fees.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
      <table class="w-full text-sm text-left" data-valuation-buckets>
        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-[#6B7280]">
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">CAPE at start</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Start years</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">4% lasted 30 years</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Median max rate</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Lowest max rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 text-[#1F2937]">
          <% @analysis.buckets.each do |bucket| %>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold"><%= bucket[:label] %></th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3"><%= bucket[:count] %></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3"><%= bucket[:survived_count] %> of <%= bucket[:count] %></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3"><%= number_with_precision(bucket[:median_swr], precision: 2) %>%</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">
                <%= number_with_precision(bucket[:worst][:max_swr], precision: 2) %>%
                (<%= link_to bucket[:worst][:year], year_detail_path(bucket[:worst][:year]), class: "text-[#7C3AED] font-medium hover:underline" %>)
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[#6B7280]">
      The two move in opposite directions: the higher the CAPE at the start, the lower the rate that lasted. The correlation is <%= number_with_precision(@analysis.correlation, precision: 2) %> on a scale from -1 to +1, where 0 means no link and -1 means they move in exact lockstep in opposite directions. <%= number_with_precision(@analysis.correlation, precision: 2) %> is a strong link, not a perfect one: starting valuation explains roughly <%= (@analysis.correlation**2 * 100).round %>% of the difference between good and bad start years.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
